\image(figures/mt64_twist.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The low bit of the joined word selects a fixed XOR correction.)
\alttext(Each panel shows 64 bit rows over join, shift, mask and result. The two joins differ only at bit zero. Their shifts agree, but the odd case spreads the fixed twist-mask pattern across the final word.)

>> Temper the tiny word one, then invert it

From x=one, the right-29 stage changes nothing. The left-17 stage gives
\(\mathtt{0000000000020001}\), the left-37 stage gives
\(\mathtt{0040002000020001}\), and the final stage gives
\(\mathtt{0040002000020801}\). Native inverse tempering recovers one exactly.
The second panel repeats the same stages for the first raw state word actually
emitted after seeding 5489; its tempered output is decimal 14514284786278117030.
Neither diagram treats tempering as a new state transition.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/mt64_temper.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  dm::random::MersenneTwister64  rng(5489);
  const auto                     first = rng.next_u64();
  const auto                     tiny  = dm::random::mt19937_64_temper_steps(1);
  const auto                     real  = dm::random::mt19937_64_temper_steps(rng.state_words()[0]);
  const std::vector<std::string> labels{"input", "R29", "L17", "L37", "R43"};
  auto a = dm::random::bit_plot(std::vector<std::uint64_t>(tiny.begin(), tiny.end()), 64)
               .title("Tempering the raw word one")
               .x_ticks({.5, 1.5, 2.5, 3.5, 4.5}, labels)
               .x_label("stage");
  auto b = dm::random::bit_plot(std::vector<std::uint64_t>(real.begin(), real.end()), 64)
               .title("First word from seed 5489")
               .x_ticks({.5, 1.5, 2.5, 3.5, 4.5}, labels)
               .x_label("stage");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(a).add(b).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/mt64_temper.svg");
  std::print("| stage | input one | first seeded word |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n");
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < labels.size(); ++i)
    std::print("| {} | {:016x} | {:016x} |\n", labels[i], tiny[i], real[i]);
  std::print(
      "\nInverse of tiny output: {}; inverse of seeded output: {:016x}.\n",
      dm::random::mt19937_64_untemper(tiny.back()),
      dm::random::mt19937_64_untemper(first));
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| stage | input one | first seeded word |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| input | 0000000000000001 | 245b1c66f2bdc210 |
| R29 | 0000000000000001 | 245b1c67f2ed8305 |
| L17 | 0000000000020001 | 149d79bcf6ef8305 |
| L37 | 0040002000020001 | c96d191cf6ef8305 |
| R43 | 0040002000020801 | c96d191cf6f6aea6 |

