\image(figures/mt64_temper.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Tempering moves information through masked shifts while retaining an exact inverse.)
\alttext(The word one develops a few distant one bits through the four stages. The first real seeded word produces a denser pattern. Every full output maps back to its raw input exactly.)

> Checking the implementation and its limits

>> Seeded reference streams, refill boundaries and sampling order

Compare eight declared seeds, including zero, the high bit and the all-ones value,
for 10000 consecutive outputs each. This exercises repeated refills in
80000 exact 64-bit word comparisons, covering 5120000 bit positions. The standard's
10000th default-seeded word is 9981545732273789042;
its scalar default seed is 5489. Our constructor requires an explicit seed.
Endpoint words and the boundary transcript are hexadecimal, with zero-based output
indices. Index 311 exhausts the first block; index 312 triggers the next refill.

The plots are descriptive views of fresh seed-5489 streams. A visually unstructured
bit raster or pair cloud does not establish independence. The final three sampler
calls preserve the original report's order: first raw word, then normal(10,2), then
an inclusive die roll. Changing that order changes which raw words are consumed.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/mt64_reference.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto table = dm::random::mt19937_64_conformance(
      {0, 1, 42, 5489, 0xffffffffULL, 0x100000000ULL, 0x8000000000000000ULL, ~std::uint64_t{0}},
      10000);
  dm::random::MersenneTwister64 bits(5489), pairs(5489), transcript(5489), sample(5489);
  std::vector<std::uint64_t>    words(128);
  for (auto& word : words)
    word = bits.next_u64();
  const auto          u = dm::random::uniform_sample(pairs, 2000);
  std::vector<double> x, y;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < u.size(); i += 2) {
    x.push_back(u[i]);
    y.push_back(u[i + 1]);
  }
  auto a = dm::random::bit_plot(words, 16).title("First 128 words: low 16 bits");
  auto b = dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
               .points(x, y, "pairs", {40, 100, 190}, 1.5)
               .title("1000 non-overlapping uniform pairs")
               .x_label("first uniform")
               .y_label("second uniform")
               .x_limits(0, 1)
               .y_limits(0, 1);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(a).add(b).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/mt64_reference.svg");
  std::print(
      "{}\n\n| output index | next block index | raw output |\n| ---: | ---: | :--- |\n",
      table.select({"seed", "draws", "mismatches", "native_first", "native_last"}).to_md(0));
  const std::set<std::size_t> show{0, 1, 155, 156, 310, 311, 312, 313, 623, 624, 9999};
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < 10000; ++i) {
    const auto word = transcript.next_u64();
    if (show.contains(i))
      std::print("| {} | {} | {:016x} |\n", i, transcript.block_index(), word);
  }
  const auto first  = sample.next_u64();
  const auto normal = sample.normal(10, 2);
  const auto die    = sample.uniform_u64(1, 6);
  std::print(
      "\nOriginal sampler transcript: first={}, normal(10,2)={:.6f}, die={}.\n",
      first,
      normal,
      die);
}
```
