// result_end
\caption(All declared raw streams match the standard engine, including many ordered refills.)
\alttext(The first 128 outputs are shown as a low-bit raster. A separate stream supplies 1000 non-overlapping uniform pairs filling the unit square; neither visual is a randomness certificate.)

>> An aligned output block is enough to reproduce the continuation

Observe all 312 full outputs beginning at a refill. Invert each to recover the
stored raw block, set the next index to 312, and apply the same ordered recurrence.
The next block is then determined. Induction gives the same result for every later
block. No seed search is involved. The native `from_output_block` factory implements
this calculation and starts with an empty normal cache; it does not recover a
previously cached normal value or infer the starting alignment.

We collect the first block from a known local engine, then freeze that recovered
state before generating 4096 unseen words. The two rasters show only the first
64 held-out words, while the error count checks all 4096. This is an exact
predictability demonstration on our own sequence, distinct from probabilistic
quality tests. Arbitrary input arrays are accepted as deterministic states; they
need not be reachable by scalar seeding. An all-zero supplied block gives a
degenerate zero continuation and is outside the nonzero-state period claim.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/mt64_recovery.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  dm::random::MersenneTwister64  source(42);
  std::array<std::uint64_t, 312> observed{};
  for (auto& word : observed)
    word = source.next_u64();
  auto                       recovered = dm::random::MersenneTwister64::from_output_block(observed);
  std::vector<std::uint64_t> actual(4096), predicted(4096);
  std::size_t                errors = 0;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < actual.size(); ++i) {
    actual[i]    = source.next_u64();
    predicted[i] = recovered.next_u64();
    errors += actual[i] != predicted[i];
  }
  auto a = dm::random::bit_plot(std::vector<std::uint64_t>(actual.begin(), actual.begin() + 64), 16)
               .title("Unseen outputs: low 16 bits");
  auto b = dm::random::bit_plot(
               std::vector<std::uint64_t>(predicted.begin(), predicted.begin() + 64), 16)
               .title("Recovered-state predictions");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(a).add(b).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/mt64_recovery.svg");
  std::print(
      "Observed full words: {}; held-out words: {}; mismatches: {}.\n\n| held-out index | actual | "
      "predicted |\n| ---: | :--- | :--- |\n",
      observed.size(),
      actual.size(),
      errors);
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < 6; ++i)
    std::print("| {} | {:016x} | {:016x} |\n", i, actual[i], predicted[i]);
}
```
